  "body": "## Summary\n\nPR2771's relative nearest-even line implementation leaves finite formats open. This proves a common grid and sufficient signed register width for its complete pinned QQ16 decoder, with arbitrary declared dyadic entry grid and exact quarter ADDs:\n\n```text\nk = b + 22 + ceil_log2(lambda) + floor(h*lambda/2)\nQmax = Q0 + 3*k + 6\nsigned component width = Qmax + E + 20\n```\n\nThe 3,816-cut certificate identifies three successive line refinements and three quarter divisions along the maximal recurrence path. For h=73, lambda=1, b=64, Q0=64, E=0, the sufficient format is 436 fractional bits and 456 signed component bits. This is an exact conservative grid envelope, not minimum necessary precision.\n\nOnly `research/qq16-finite-dyadic-format/` is added. The proof defines unlimited arithmetic first, inherits the pinned completed-error theorem, and then shows finite registers simulate it without overflow or underflow. Direct loops retain their scan, arithmetic, rounding and movement liabilities; no recursive rank-one price is inherited.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: PR2771 uses exact rational arithmetic and explicitly leaves finite formats open. After: the written quantified proof, source-bound grid recurrence and checked integer reference give an explicit format under the stated entry norm/grid assumptions.\n- Normal and optimized registered CPython 3.12.15 replay pass on macOS arm64, plus optimized CPython 3.14.7 replay. Checks cover all 3,816 changed-field cuts, 412,128 independent scalar recurrence comparisons, 54 rounded-line cases with nonzero errors and 12 complete-word isometry fixtures. Ten semantic controls and five artifact test groups pass, including source/typed-receipt corruption and a read-only Git-free export.\n- Research-workflow suite: 67 passed, seven Linux-only process-tree checks skipped on macOS. Ruff lint/format, metadata/source pins and whitespace checks pass. Separate internal proof/artifact reviews found no substantive defect; no independent human or formal-kernel review is claimed.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -Werror -I -B scripts/research_package.py \\\n  --package research/qq16-finite-dyadic-format\n```\n\nScientific base: canonical main `db3edc00f732806f663bfb9d4000567f18b17386`, priority revision 5. Exact consumed PR2771 head is `e707681c3f6db70d0432501403e2122794a36ade`, retaining ywz65's PR2707 word and Nick Petalas's PR2736 error proof. TASK/SOURCES record source pins, current-main compatibility and final overlap coverage. [Canonical investigation](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2727#discussioncomment-18960034).\n\nCredit ywz65/PR2707/2540, Arham Tahir/PR2681, Nick Petalas/PR2771/2736, Ali Romman and the retained QQ16/native/geometry lineage. Ross Richardson's public floor-grid and reversible-lifting artifacts in Discussion2727 already give related rounding and finite-capacity results. This contribution adds the relative-scale denominator-depth bound with arbitrary entry grid and exact quarters, not the first whole-word range argument. Original proof notices are preserved; new material is Apache-2.0.\n\nThe actual native/frame semantics and prior error constants are inherited. The complete-word fixtures exercise the isometry contract rather than reconstruct actual cover routing. Entry/F0/B1 precision, recursively cheap arithmetic, physical movement/hosting, bit/tape/control costs, output consumption and supplier admission remain open. No selected cold replay, hosted-CI pass, new kappa or selected-frontier change is claimed. Family decision: narrow and stop at this arithmetic format lemma.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** research\n\nOne opt-in package. Existing verifiers, frozen predecessor inputs and selected records are unchanged.\n",
